export const POSTS = [{"id":"x8shTwhQXXdKsB1QyomO","slug":"light-bulb-the-glowing-invention-that-gave-us-the-night","title":"Light bulb: The glowing invention that gave us the night","excerpt":"Imagine doing your homework in total darkness! Long ago, people only had candles and fires to see at night. Then inventors made a glowing glass ball that change","content":"<div class=\"lesson-note\">\n  <div class=\"ln-headline\">\n    <div class=\"ln-kicker\">Invention Facts · Grade 2</div>\n    <h1 class=\"ln-h1\">Banishing the Dark: <em>The Light Bulb</em></h1>\n    <p class=\"ln-lede\">Imagine doing your homework in total darkness! Long ago, people only had candles and fires to see at night. Then inventors made a glowing glass ball that changed our world forever.</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-byline\">\n    <strong>Prep Portal Science Desk</strong><span class=\"ln-byline-dot\">·</span>\n    <span>Electricity · Inventions · Light</span><span class=\"ln-byline-dot\">·</span>\n    <span class=\"ln-level-badge\">Grade 2</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-facts-strip\">\n    <div class=\"ln-facts-label\">Quick Facts</div>\n    <div class=\"ln-facts-grid\">\n      <div class=\"ln-fact-item\"><div class=\"ln-fact-num\">Thomas Edison</div><div class=\"ln-fact-text\">He built a famous light bulb in 1879 that burned for 1,500 hours.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"ln-fact-item\"><div class=\"ln-fact-num\">Super Hot</div><div class=\"ln-fact-text\">The wire inside an old bulb can reach 2,500 degrees Celsius!</div></div>\n      <div class=\"ln-fact-item\"><div class=\"ln-fact-num\">Fast Light</div><div class=\"ln-fact-text\">Electricity travels into your bulb in less than 1 second.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-article-body\">\n    <div class=\"ln-col\">\n      <span class=\"ln-h2\">Meet the Light Bulb</span>\n      <p class=\"ln-p\">Look around your house in Lagos or Abuja. You will see a small <span class=\"ln-chip blue\">glass bulb</span> sitting on your ceiling. It has a rounded glass body and a metal bottom. Inside, there is a tiny wire that shines brightly when power comes on. It uses <span class=\"ln-chip blue\">electricity</span> to bring daylight into our rooms after sunset!</p>\n      <div class=\"ln-pull-quote\"><span class=\"ln-quote-mark\">\"</span><p>A light bulb turns invisible power into bright sunshine inside your house!</p></div>\n      <span class=\"ln-h2\">How It Glows Like Magic</span>\n      <p class=\"ln-p\">Electricity moves through wires like danfo buses moving down a road. When you flip the switch, power rushes into the bulb. It squeezes through a tiny wire called a <span class=\"ln-chip red\">filament</span>. The tiny wire gets super hot like a pot of boiling jollof. Because it is so hot, it begins to glow brightly! The clear glass keeps the air away so the wire does not burn up.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><span class=\"ln-chip green\">Filament</span> - The thin wire inside that glows when hot.</li>\n        <li><span class=\"ln-chip green\">Switch</span> - The button you press to start electricity.</li>\n        <li><span class=\"ln-chip green\">Glass Globe</span> - The glass shell that protects the wire inside.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"ln-col\">\n      <span class=\"ln-h2\">Why The Light Bulb Matters</span>\n      <p class=\"ln-p\">Before light bulbs, night time was very dark and tricky. People used oil lamps that made dark smoke. Candles could easily fall and start bad fires. Today, light bulbs help doctors work in hospitals at night. Children can read books and play games long after the sun goes down.</p>\n      <ol class=\"ln-process-list\">\n        <li><span class=\"ln-process-title\">Step 1 - Flip the Switch.</span><br>You press the wall button to clear the path for energy.</li>\n        <li><span class=\"ln-process-title\">Step 2 - Power Rushes In.</span><br>Electricity zooms through the lamp wire into the bulb base.</li>\n        <li><span class=\"ln-process-title\">Step 3 - The Wire Glows.</span><br>The tiny filament heats up quickly and lights your room!</li>\n      </ol>\n      <div class=\"ln-pull-quote\"><span class=\"ln-quote-mark\">\"</span><p>Light bulbs let market stalls stay open late into the evening!</p></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-table-section\">\n    <div class=\"ln-table-title\">Light Bulb vs. Candle</div>\n    <table class=\"ln-table\">\n      <thead><tr><th></th><th>Light Bulb</th><th>Candle</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Body</td><td>Glass globe with a wire inside</td><td>Stick made of soft wax</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Smoke</td><td>Clean and smokeless</td><td>Makes dark smoke and wax drops</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Wind test</td><td>Stays bright in strong wind</td><td>Blows out easily in the breeze</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Turning on</td><td>Flip a simple wall switch</td><td>Must light with a matchstick</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-features\">\n    <div class=\"ln-features-title\">Imagine If You Invented It</div>\n    <div class=\"ln-features-grid\">\n      <div class=\"ln-feature-card\"><div class=\"ln-feature-num\">Idea 1</div><div class=\"ln-feature-label\">Rainbow Bulb</div><div class=\"ln-feature-desc\">You make a bulb that changes color when you shout. It turns green when your team scores a goal!</div></div>\n      <div class=\"ln-feature-card\"><div class=\"ln-feature-num\">Idea 2</div><div class=\"ln-feature-label\">Sun Catcher</div><div class=\"ln-feature-desc\">This special bulb drinks up sunlight during the day. It shines all night even when the generator goes off!</div></div>\n      <div class=\"ln-feature-card\"><div class=\"ln-feature-num\">Idea 3</div><div class=\"ln-feature-label\">Bouncy Light</div><div class=\"ln-feature-desc\">Make a light bulb out of soft rubbery glass. If it falls on the floor, it bounces like a football!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-activity\">\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"ln-activity-label\">Try This</div>\n      <p class=\"ln-activity-text\"><strong>Shadow Puppets with Torchlight.</strong> Ask an adult for a small flashlight or phone light in a dark room. Point the light at a smooth wall. Move your hands in front of the beam to make dog or bird shapes! Notice how light travels straight until your hands stop it.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-table-section\">\n    <div class=\"ln-table-title\">Check Your Understanding</div>\n    <table class=\"ln-table\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Think about it</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>What is the thin wire inside a light bulb called?</td><td>It is called a filament.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Why does the thin wire start to shine?</td><td>It gets super hot when electricity passes through it.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Why is a light bulb safer than a fire candle?</td><td>It has no open flame and does not create smoke.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>What keeps the thin wire inside from burning up?</td><td>The glass ball keeps fresh air away from the hot wire.</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ln-table-section\">\n    <div class=\"ln-table-title\">Vocabulary Builder</div>\n    <table class=\"ln-table\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Word</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td><strong>Filament</strong></td><td>A very thin wire inside a light bulb that shines when hot.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>Electricity</strong></td><td>A form of power that travels along wires to run lamps and TVs.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>Invention</strong></td><td>A brand new thing made to solve a daily problem.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>Glow</strong></td><td>To give off a bright and steady light.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><strong>Energy</strong></td><td>The strength needed to move things or make light and heat.</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n</div>","subject":"inventions","classLevel":"primary-2","featuredImage":null,"videoLink":null,"practiceLink":null,"publishedAt":1793948941092,"modelUsed":"Gemini (server)"}];
